  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p13-q14-instruction",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Determine, without using a calculator, which is the greater number in each pair.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$2\\sqrt{3}$ or $\\sqrt{11}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\sqrt{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2\\sqrt{3})^2&=12\\\\(\\sqrt{11})^2&=11\\end{align*}$$\nBoth numbers are positive and $12>11$, so $2\\sqrt{3}>\\sqrt{11}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$7\\sqrt{2}$ or $3\\sqrt{11}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3\\sqrt{11}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(7\\sqrt{2})^2&=98\\\\(3\\sqrt{11})^2&=99\\end{align*}$$\nBoth numbers are positive and $99>98$, so $3\\sqrt{11}>7\\sqrt{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$3+2\\sqrt{2}$ or $15-7\\sqrt{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3+2\\sqrt{2}$\n\nTheir difference is $9\\sqrt{2}-12>0$, since $(9\\sqrt{2})^2=162>144=12^2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(3+2\\sqrt{2})-(15-7\\sqrt{2})&=9\\sqrt{2}-12\\\\(9\\sqrt{2})^2&=162\\\\12^2&=144\\end{align*}$$\nSince $9\\sqrt{2}$ and $12$ are positive and $162>144$, we have $9\\sqrt{2}>12$. The difference is positive, so $3+2\\sqrt{2}$ is greater.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q14-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$2\\sqrt{6}-3$ or $7-2\\sqrt{6}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$7-2\\sqrt{6}$\n\nIts difference from the other number is $10-4\\sqrt{6}>0$, since $10^2=100>96=(4\\sqrt{6})^2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(7-2\\sqrt{6})-(2\\sqrt{6}-3)&=10-4\\sqrt{6}\\\\10^2&=100\\\\(4\\sqrt{6})^2&=96\\end{align*}$$\nSince $10$ and $4\\sqrt{6}$ are positive and $100>96$, we have $10>4\\sqrt{6}$. The difference is positive, so $7-2\\sqrt{6}$ is greater.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
